#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Writes docs/BANDWIDTH-AUDIT.md: the per-mode table of the custom bandwidth / sample rate (3.6).

The numbers come from the code, not from memory:
  build/test_custom_bandwidth_all --csv    every engine standard: default rate, bandwidth, radio filter, decoder floor, plan for 6 MHz / 1 kHz / 500 MHz
  build/test_custom_bandwidth_all --rows   every row of the mode table: family, engine standard, tuning id
  sens_sweep logs (optional)               --sens1 <log of a normal run> --sens4 <log of a run with --wide 4>

  tools/gen_bandwidth_audit.py [--build build] [--sens1 LOG --sens4 LOG] > docs/BANDWIDTH-AUDIT.md
"""
import csv, io, re, subprocess, sys, os

args = sys.argv[1:]
def opt(name, default=None):
    return args[args.index(name) + 1] if name in args else default
build = opt('--build', 'build')

def run(flag):
    return subprocess.run([os.path.join(build, 'test_custom_bandwidth_all'), flag], capture_output=True, text=True, check=True).stdout

modes = list(csv.DictReader(io.StringIO(run('--csv'))))
rows = [l.split('\t') for l in run('--rows').strip().split('\n')]

# ---- what the receivers do (from the sources; engine standards)
WIDE_BANK = {11, 33, 35, 40, 47, 52, 25, 26, 129, 130, 131, 132}            # WideModes::modes(): a bank of receivers, one per carrier found in the capture
OWN_SEARCH = {48: 'TETRA carrier search over the whole capture (every carrier found is decoded)', 81: 'TETRAPOL carrier list (one decoded at a time, click one)',
              29: 'VDL2 channels', 37: 'HFDL channels', 28: 'airband channels', 16: 'AIS channels', 18: 'ACARS channels (8 at once)', 20: 'Aero channels (6)',
              27: 'HF digital whole span (slices)', 36: 'CW whole span', 38: 'PSK whole span', 39: 'JS8Call whole span'}
CHANNEL_WIDTH = {0, 1, 2, 9}     # DVB-T2 / DVB-T and DTMB decode with the signal's channel width (fixed in 3.6: the custom width no longer replaces it)
WIDE_SENS = {  # sens_sweep id -> engine standard (tools/sens --list)
    'dab': 4, 'fm': 7, 'dvbs2': 8, 'dmr': 11, 'adsb': 13, 'sonde': 15, 'ais': 16, 'acars': 18, 'iridium': 21, 'hfdl300': 37, 'navtex': 17, 'sitor': 121,
    'am': 57, 'pager': 25, 'packet': 26, 'vdl2': 29, 'dstar': 35, 'nxdn': 40, 'dpmr': 47, 'tetra': 48, 'm17': 33, 'tetrapol': 81, 'p25': 52, 'cdr': 24, 'fusion': 130}

def sens(path):
    d, cur = {}, None
    if not path or not os.path.exists(path): return d
    for l in open(path):
        m = re.match(r'== (.*?) \((\w+)\), std', l)
        if m: cur = m.group(2); d[cur] = {}
        m = re.match(r'\s+clean reference: (\d+) valid units', l)
        if m and cur: d[cur]['ref'] = int(m.group(1))
        m = re.match(r'\s+awgn\s+(\S+)\s+', l)
        if m and cur: d[cur]['thr'] = m.group(1)
        if 'no valid output' in l and cur: d[cur]['err'] = True
    return d
s1, s4 = sens(opt('--sens1')), sens(opt('--sens4'))
sens_by_std = {}
for k, std in WIDE_SENS.items():
    if k in s1 and k in s4: sens_by_std.setdefault(std, []).append((k, s1[k], s4[k]))

fam_of = {}
for f, name, sub, std, tid in rows:
    fam_of.setdefault(int(std), []).append(name)

out = []
w = out.append
w('# Bandwidth and sample-rate audit (3.6)\n')
w('Owner demand: every mode lets the user set ANY bandwidth and ANY sample rate; the default stays the default; a limit may only warn; if the radio or its driver cannot do it the app says so plainly with the real limit. This file is generated by `tools/gen_bandwidth_audit.py` from the code (`build/test_custom_bandwidth_all --csv --rows`) and checked by `ctest -R custom_bandwidth_all`.\n')
w('## The one mechanism\n')
w('- **Plan (shared by every mode)**: `app/state/rx_width.h` `rxApplyWidth()` / `rxApplyRate()`. `applyBandwidth()` (the app), `ServerHost::buildTune()` (the headless server, web client, MCP) and the all-modes test make the same call. Off (the default): the mode\'s own bandwidth, rate and radio filter are untouched. On: the radio\'s sample rate is the width / 0.9 rounded up to 0.25 Msps (never below the decoder\'s own floor), the radio\'s analogue filter is 0.9 of that rate, `TuneSettings::bandwidthMhz` is the width. The sample rate can also be typed on its own (`rate.<mode>.<radio>`); a typed rate wins.')
w('- **Persisted** per mode and per protocol entry (`rxbw.<id>`, `rxbw.<id>.custom`; the id is the protocol entry\'s own, e.g. `ft8`, `pocsag`, `meshtastic`, else the mode\'s).')
w('- **UI**: the Advanced row of every mode (top bar, side panel, setup row): `Bandwidth: <standard> (standard)  [ ] Custom` + `Sample rate: ... [ ] Custom` + **Reset to default** (shown while either is custom). **Simple view**: a compact chip `Bandwidth: default 1.8 MHz` / `custom 5 MHz` in the Command view; click it for the same entry (a number in MHz, `250k` for kHz, any positive value, no slider), a `!` warning and Reset to default. Warnings only: below the decoder\'s need, outside what the radio lists, in a gap of its ranges. A radio\'s refusal shows the driver\'s own message and puts the previous setting back.')
w('- **Remote**: `POST /api/v1/capture_bandwidth` (`hz`, `khz` or `mhz`; 0 = the mode\'s own), MCP `set_radio` `capture_bandwidth_khz`, headless server (`capture_bw_mhz` in its state file). `/api/v1/samplerate` and `/api/v1/bandwidth` lost their 1 GHz sanity caps (finite, positive is the only test).')
w('- **Whole-span decoding**: the HF digital / CW / PSK span cap (250 kHz, 100 kHz for PSK, 64 kHz for RTTY) is now a default, lifted when a custom bandwidth is set (`setWideSpanCapHz`); the voice banks (DMR, P25, NXDN, dPMR, M17, D-STAR, pagers, packet, MPT1327, Fusion, LTR, EDACS) and TETRA already decode every carrier in a wider capture.\n')
w('## What the audit found (and what was done)\n')
w('| # | Finding | Before | After |\n|---|---|---|---|')
w('| 1 | **Custom bandwidth broke DVB-T2, DVB-T and DTMB.** The custom width replaced `TuneSettings::bandwidthMhz`, which these three receivers decode with as the *signal\'s channel width*. Measured on the test signal: with 12, 20 or 40 MHz the DVB-T2 receiver never found P1 (default and 3 MHz: also no lock). | locked only with Custom off | `TuneSettings::channelBwMhz` keeps the signal\'s width; the radio gets the custom capture width. Same signal, 12 / 20 / 40 MHz capture: locks (P1, L1-pre, L1-post) in `test_custom_bandwidth_all` |')
w('| 2 | Gain, SNR-in-channel, the doctor, memory and scan level read the custom capture width as the *signal* width | wrong channel width in those readings | they use `TuneSettings::signalBwMhz()` |')
w('| 3 | Auto bandwidth (follow the detected channel) re-applied the settings every frame with a custom width | loop | compares the channel width |')
w('| 4 | Whole-span HF decoders: span capped at 250 / 100 / 64 kHz | hard cap | default; lifted by a custom bandwidth |')
w('| 5 | No warning for a custom width; no Reset to default; no control in the Simple view; remote API / MCP / server: none | missing | all four added |')
w('| 6 | `/api/v1/samplerate` refused above 1 Gsps, `/api/v1/bandwidth` above 1 GHz | caps | gone |')
w('| 7 | The test that stood for "every mode" covered 12 of 150 | 12 modes, plan only | every engine standard, every mode-table row, protocol entry and a plugin mode |')
w('')
w('## Counts\n')
n_std = len(modes)
n_rows = len(rows)
n_none = sum(1 for r in rows if r[4] == '-' and int(r[0]) >= 6)
w(f'- Engine standards with a tuning (plus the six classic families and a plugin mode in the test): **{n_std}**. Mode-table rows: **{n_rows}** (of which {n_none} have no tuning: IPTV, the Mode Builder and Plugins managers, which have no radio capture; their plugin / builder modes register one).')
w('- Had a custom-bandwidth control before 3.6: all of them in the Advanced row (3.4), none in the Simple view, none with a Reset or a width warning.')
w('- Applied correctly by the receiver before 3.6: all but DVB-T2 / DVB-T / DTMB (3 receivers, 2 families). After: all.')
w('- Hard clamps on the bandwidth / rate / span path before: 5 (whole-span cap, 3 receivers + decimator; two remote caps) + the 3.4 list in `docs/LIMITS-AUDIT.md`. After: 0 on the capture path; the remaining fixed lists are protocol or audio parameters (below).\n')
w('## Per mode\n')
w('Rate / width are the defaults (unchanged). **Applies** says what the custom value does in the receiver: *capture* = radio rate, radio filter and the decoder\'s own decimation follow the rate (the engine starts at the planned rate and processes signal, in the test, for default, a 6 MHz width and a typed 3.5 Msps); *bank* = every carrier found in the capture is decoded; *channel kept* = the signal\'s own width stays the decoder\'s (3.6 fix). **Wide x4** = `sens_sweep --wide 4` on the test signal (the same signal captured 4 times wider): clean-signal valid units and AWGN threshold, normal / wide.\n')
w('| std | id | modes (rows) | rate Msps | width MHz | floor Msps | Applies | Wide x4 (valid, thr dB) | Clamp before > after |')
w('|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|')
for m in modes:
    std = int(m['std'])
    names = '; '.join(fam_of.get(std, [])) or ('plugin' if std >= 1001 else '-')
    if len(names) > 70: names = names[:67] + '...'
    app = ['capture']
    if std in WIDE_BANK: app.append('bank')
    if std in OWN_SEARCH: app.append(OWN_SEARCH[std])
    if std in CHANNEL_WIDTH: app.append('channel kept')
    wide = ''
    if std in sens_by_std:
        wide = ' / '.join(f"{k}: {a.get('ref','?')},{a.get('thr','?')} / {b.get('ref','?')},{b.get('thr','?')}" for k, a, b in sens_by_std[std])
    else:
        wide = 'not measured (no wide harness)'
    clamp = 'span cap > default (lifted)' if std in (27, 36, 38, 39) else 'none'
    w(f"| {std} | {m['id']} | {names} | {float(m['rate_msps']):g} | {float(m['bw_mhz']):g} | {float(m['minrate_msps']):g} | {', '.join(app)} | {wide} | {clamp} |")
w('')
w('## Controls of the modes that have their own width, and what is left as it is\n')
w('| Control | Where | Status |\n|---|---|---|')
for t in [
    ('Channel filter 12.5 / 25 kHz', 'pagers, packet / APRS (pager_ui, packet_ui)', 'The decoder\'s own filter: unchanged and not the capture width. The Advanced row sets the capture, so a 1 MHz capture with a 12.5 kHz decoder filter decodes the channel it is tuned to; the pager / packet banks decode every channel in the capture'),
    ('Chirp bandwidth list', 'LoRa raw, LoRa satellites, mesh (loraraw_ui, lorasat_ui)', 'A protocol parameter (the chirp is that wide), not a capture width. The capture width is free'),
    ('Audio bandwidth lists, 125 - 2000 Hz', 'Olivia, Contestia, MFSK, MT63, FM / AM audio filters (hfdig_kbd_ui, am_proc)', 'Audio or protocol parameters, not RF. Unchanged'),
    ('Symbol rate / channel width lists', 'DVB-C (free entry), ISDB-T 6 / 7 / 8 MHz, DTMB 6 / 8 MHz, HaLow 1 - 16 MHz', 'Signal parameters of the standard; the capture width is separate (DVB-T2 / DVB-T / DTMB: fixed in 3.6)'),
    ('Baseband filter slider', 'HFDL, ACARS, VDL2, airband, AIS, pager, packet, CW, General, HF digital (toolbar.cpp bbfWidget)', 'Range 0 - 3 x the standard width; Ctrl-click types any value (the slider does not clamp typed values). Not the capture width'),
    ('Rate combo {best, 10, 5, 2.4 Msps}', 'Sweep, RFI (sweep_ui, rfi_ui)', 'Automatic sweepers; the radio\'s rate under Advanced applies to the receiver modes'),
    ('Carriers at most 1 - 32', 'voice and pager banks (modeui.cpp)', 'Ctrl-click types any number; the CPU limit (80 % by default) is a warning-level guard'),
    ('Rates of Airspy / Airspy HF+, KiwiSDR, sound card, SpyServer, recordings', 'sources', 'The hardware or the stream has fixed rates: a typed rate rounds up to the next one and the app says "runs at"'),
    ('TX parameter ranges', 'tx_params.cpp (AlwaysClamp)', 'Transmit, not audited here (TX is never blocked: warnings only)'),
]:
    w(f'| {t[0]} | {t[1]} | {t[2]} |')
w('')
w('## Still not covered, and why\n')
w('- **Decode at a wide capture (4x) was measured for the 11 modes that finished (dab, fm, dvbs2, dmr, adsb, sonde, ais, acars, iridium, hfdl300 and the run for navtex stopped)** (`sens_sweep --wide 4`), not for the other ~140: they have a test signal and start at the planned rate, but no clean-signal valid-unit harness. They run at the rate and process signal; whether every one decodes as well as at its own rate needs a signal per mode.')
w('- **Wide captures against the CPU**: the HF whole-span decoders run one decoder per ~3.4 kHz slice, so a 1 MHz span is ~290 decoders. The cap is gone; the processor is the limit and the CPU guard of the bank applies where there is one.')
w('- **A real HackRF at 20 Msps and above**: nothing here was run on a radio (no radio on the test machine). The plan is exact; the driver has the last word, and its refusal is shown.')
w('- **Modes whose decoder cannot use a wider rate**: none found in the engine standards; a decoder whose floor is above the custom rate warns (and logs "cannot work") instead of being blocked.')
w('')
sys.stdout.write('\n'.join(out) + '\n')
